PARAPHRASED: A1's existing floor and inhabitance. floor_oneHistory_member still rejects a World with height greater than steps or the wrong origin. It does not test structurally valid rollback or unauthorized adoption. inhabited_audited still exhibits an audited rotate without a Reach execution from a member-chosen start. The new inhabited_agree_pageAbsorbs does exhibit a real follower step from genesis to the batch's next World. That answers the narrower missing example of page absorption. It does not repair the continuity quantifiers.

PARAPHRASED: one history between members. OneHistory.pair remains equality of endpoint Worlds conditional on a common start, equal step counts, and equal chains. It still permits isolated divergent histories with unequal chains. The new ForkConsistent and ForkConsistent.sync are stronger than that lemma. They range over S.follow and conclude equality of log prefixes. The post theorem applies only when the compared position lies strictly after the follower's old position and no later than its new position. Its refusal arm carries an existential mismatch witness. The sync theorem applies only when a frame crosses the supplied anchor from below. Its conclusion excludes a different prefix at that anchor unless the listed hash inputs collide. These are actual comparison theorems over the deployed command step.

OWED: the full comparison contract. Both new fork theorems assume folds from the same g. A1 still does not establish that common trusted start. The sync theorem assumes that the continuation contains the intended anchor. It does not authenticate the source of that anchor. Neither theorem covers an already-passed anchor or missing retained evidence. The post theorem excludes posts beyond the page's end. Host.Follow.behindOr returns the original output when its retained-chain lookup produces no comparison. That behavior is not an explicit successful consistency proof. The post theorem also permits the page to be retained before the mismatch is reported. Its mathematical witness is not an exported certificate accusing the writer. Command.refused drops the post's step and member information from the reply bytes. A member attestation is not automatically attributable writer equivocation. SPEC-19 names these trust cases but supplies no distinct price for completing them. The older section 11.1 estimate starts from the stale assertion that members never compare heads. It does not price the remaining work.

ANSWERED: finite page-acceptance completeness at the command-step boundary. Agree.pageAbsorbs proves that a bounded batch's staged events move the deployed follower to the batch's resulting World when supplied as the specified page. The premises require canonical rows, a canonical call codec, the same starting World, and a phase-2 continuation without an anchor. The page's events, chain, endpoint, and tip are supplied by equalities to the staged batch. The deaf follower is refuted by this statement. The deployed rotate page inhabits it. This is the finite input-output theorem requested in the first review. The proof does not require a liveness promise.

OWED: delivery of that honest page by the deployed writer. Agree.pageAbsorbs does not prove that the pager reads the records staged by admitBatch. It does not establish persistence of the batch or delivery of a sequence of pages. SPEC-20 names the pager gap explicitly. The gap belongs in the Store trace and recovery work. Calling the premise “the writer's page” must not hide that missing composition.

ANSWERED: the objection to an endpoint-only authority predicate. Integrity.authority quantifies over StepAt at each position of the actual audited log. It covers a changed cell that was live immediately before that step. A change followed by restoration remains covered. Deletion of a previously live cell remains covered. The object floor exhibits a non-owner write against this deployed claim. The first review's endpoint objection does not apply to this landed statement.

PARAPHRASED: authority confinement for every accepted effect. Births are outside Integrity.authority. Nested authorization is stated at the dispatched actor without a composed account of that actor's authority back to the signed request. Several Authorized constructors leave the resulting cell unrestricted. Authorized.account takes an arbitrary after. AccountMove identifies a transfer or credit leg and its authority without equating the resulting balance change to the requested amount. A transfer of 1 is not required by this predicate to change balances by 1. Authorized.member identifies an authorized rotate without specifying the resulting member cell. The aggregate value theorem does not supply those missing local postconditions. SPEC-19's claim that the authority and value clauses compose today is too broad. Its “weeks per clause” price omits these effect-correspondence obligations.

PARAPHRASED: value integrity. Integrity.value still proves aggregate balance conservation and conditional floor conservation. The floor exception still tests membership in createdIds rather than an independently stated issuance rule. w.Canon remains a premise. The top-level member-start predicate does not establish it for all allowed pins. The minting floor still tests the balance clause. The existing issue/account/transfer witness still demonstrates real movement rather than authority confinement. The first review's distinction between a legitimate mutation endpoint and a vacuous premise remains unchanged.

ANSWERED: the absence of a separate deployed grant-cap theorem. Integrity.grantCap now bounds the selected transfer amounts and credit amounts along the system's own step chain. CellsCanon and LedgerContiguous are explicit premises. The capless transfer and credit floors exercise both ledgers. The formal quantification selects at most one dispatched amount per step. Reading this as the total of every nested move requires the accompanying uniqueness or aggregation argument. The README's claim that every follower-reached World supplies LedgerContiguous also needs qualification by the trusted-start case. A lemma about honest extensions does not establish the invariant for arbitrary pinned bytes.


OWED: deployment wiring. System remains a record of independent component functions. Updating receive does not make follow call the replacement. Updating admit does not make submit call the replacement. Host.Main delegates to Host.Cli.main. The serve and follow branches assemble their loops from concrete definitions outside Spec.System. A theorem that main calls the record's handle and follow fields would close the selection-drift gap for those calls. It would not establish that the selected follow uses the selected kernel fields. It would not establish any ordering between a durable append and an observable reply. It would not establish refinement to the independent contract.

The closure criterion is a theorem about the actual program's observable traces under named effect contracts. That theorem must follow the real entry-point dispatch, startup and recovery paths, loop state, calls, and effects. One implementation route is to assemble the callers from shared primitive operations in a module used by production. A second route is to retain concrete callers and prove their connection to the execution relation. Making main take System is not intrinsically required by either route. A proof-facing record of unrelated functions is not sufficient for either route. An effect program interpreted by both production IO and the crash model would make this connection easier to maintain. A small interpreter's conformance would then be an explicit proof obligation or trusted boundary. Compiler, FFI, filesystem, transport, and custody assumptions must be stated at their actual interfaces.

SPEC-19 prices the entry-point change at days and the effect interpreter at a month. Days is a plausible scope for replacing duplicated selection sites with shared assembly. It is not a price for proving the composed system. The durable trace also needs pager provenance, checkpoint and adoption behavior, restart invariants, asynchronous sealing, and observable failure outcomes. The entry-point theorem and those semantic obligations need separate completion criteria. Treating their sum as a wiring theorem underprices the gap.

PARAPHRASED: the first adopted apex. It is prose in SPEC-19 and the README. No Lean declaration states observable-execution refinement to an intent-indexed durable contract. Its strongest available support consists of separate signing, settlement, page-agreement, recovery, volume, and Bell claims. No composition relates their events to one execution or one intent. Continuation decoding and planning supply the command for the consent slices. Kept and the recovery procedure supply the recovered-state interpretation. Stable, Fresh, Live, and Crash supply resident persistence. Runs and TicksWith supply the Bell effect histories. These premises do the work that an actual process invariant must eventually discharge. The quarter-scale price names the right major work areas but does not replace the missing trace relation.

PARAPHRASED: the second adopted apex. It is prose rather than a theorem about every accepted transition. The strongest support combines per-step live-cell authority, aggregate value conservation, selected grant spending, package-specific exchange and escrow properties, and NoRef law chains. Audited supplies kernel decision provenance. Canonical-state and ledger-contiguity premises supply the representation invariants. Dispatched supplies nested operational provenance. NoRef and the every-entry in-force premise restrict the semantic law conclusion. Program equality fixes the exchange and escrow interpreter. Births, exact local effects, changing laws, contextual evaluation, and resource adequacy remain outside the composed promise. Weeks per clause is not an honest completion price until those clauses are stated.

PARAPHRASED: the third adopted apex. It is prose rather than a theorem covering all accepted views and foreign receipts. The strongest member result is still endpoint recoverability from some Start under keyFaithful. The strongest comparison results now identify equal prefixes at an in-page comparison. The strongest foreign result assumes the folded source World and its root binding. The common g, the crossed-position inequalities, and HeadOf supply the missing continuity and source-history connections. The collision alternatives expose cryptographic exceptions without authenticating authority. None of these statements supplies the advertised combination of an explicitly trusted start and checkable writer equivocation evidence.

Before calling the top-level spec complete, I require formal versions of all three apex contracts with the deployed-process refinement proved. The intent contract must follow one authenticated intent through retries, signing, settlement, cancellation, persistence, and restart. The transition contract must cover births, exact authorized effects, issuance, delegated spending, applicable contextual laws, and the declared resource budget. The view contract must retain the authorized start and distinguish verified comparison, unavailable evidence, and attributable equivocation. Foreign receipts must use an explicitly selected validity source with an independently authenticated authority binding. The Bell must instantiate the durable intent contract over a ring life at the provider's charging boundary. Every surviving explanatory sentence must agree with those theorem statements.

The project is closer to a reviewable trusted statement than it was in the first review because it now exposes more component obligations, but completion still requires the three apex refinement theorems over the actual deployed executions.

